    {
      "id": "22ac6062-693c-4476-8897-fb805f4768e9",
      "name": "Sticky Note 7e60c367",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## Google Review Reply Drafter\n**Never leave a Google review unanswered again.**\n\n### How it works\n1. Every hour, new Google reviews are fetched for your location.\n2. Reviews already in your sheet are skipped.\n3. An AI model rates sentiment and urgency and drafts an on-brand reply.\n4. Each review and draft is saved in Google Sheets.\n5. The draft is emailed to you for approval. Reviews of 3 stars or less are marked URGENT.\n6. Optional: turn on auto-posting to publish replies directly."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3abf90c0-25f0-4dda-b6be-70c3805878f7",
      "name": "Sticky Note 076da1f2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## Setup (about 15 minutes)\n1. Create a Google Sheet with two tabs named `Reviews` and `Errors`.\n2. Type these headers in row 1, exactly as written:\n   - **Reviews:** Review ID, Date, Reviewer, Rating, Comment, Sentiment, Urgency, Draft Reply, Status\n   - **Errors:** Timestamp, Node, Error, Execution ID\n3. Connect credentials: Google OAuth2 (scope `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/business.manage`), Google Sheets OAuth2, Gmail OAuth2 and OpenRouter.\n4. Fill in **Workflow Settings**.\n5. Run once manually to test, then activate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "dfb62f4a-ca81-4ede-9d07-b60d223b5830",
      "name": "Sticky Note a00505d4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -32,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 424,
        "content": "## 1. Load settings and logged reviews\nYour business details are set and the review IDs already in the sheet are read so nothing is processed twice.\n\n**You need to:** fill in business name, owner email, account ID, location ID, sheet ID and brand voice in **Workflow Settings**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "de94f2b1-185d-48e3-8560-20778dff64b6",
      "name": "Sticky Note b5f4a103",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        688,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## 2. Fetch and filter reviews\nThe Google Business Profile API returns the latest reviews. Only new reviews without an existing owner reply move on.\n\n**You need to:** connect a Google OAuth2 credential with the business.manage scope."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "68af3764-0a24-4e1a-987d-5294a222486f",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4856f3a4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1168,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 632,
        "content": "## 3. AI classifies and drafts the reply\nThe AI returns sentiment, urgency, a summary and a reply under 90 words. The code node checks the answer and uses a safe default reply if the output is broken.\n\n**You need to:** add your OpenRouter credential and pick any chat model that can return JSON."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5f92fd7a-a58e-49f4-b062-2213aacd87d1",
      "name": "Sticky Note d2bbaadf",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1648,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 424,
        "content": "## 4. Log and send for approval\nEvery review is added to the `Reviews` tab, then the draft is emailed to you. 3 stars or less gets an URGENT subject.\n\n**You need to:** create the `Reviews` tab with the exact headers and connect Gmail."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "185da4d2-cc17-43c7-94b5-a78ffdcce954",
      "name": "Sticky Note 60bad89d",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2128,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 504,
        "content": "## 5. Optional auto-posting\nOff by default. When on, the reply is published to Google through the updateReply endpoint.\n\n**You need to:** set `autoPostReplies` to true in **Workflow Settings** only after you trust the drafts."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a0bb6c84-f8f5-44f4-836b-7b456884c047",
      "name": "Sticky Note b826e757",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1648,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 424,
        "content": "## 6. Error handling\nIf fetching, emailing or posting fails, the error is saved in the `Errors` tab and emailed to you with the node and execution ID.\n\n**You need to:** create the `Errors` tab with the headers Timestamp, Node, Error, Execution ID."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
